Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Silica Shattering Upward
- Story & Context: Silas found a shard of annealed glass embedded in a fiber optic junction near the Mid-Atlantic Ridge, a reminder of the pressure that nearly collapsed the station. As the alarm sirens began to wail, he realized the glass was vibrating in perfect sync with his modular synth patch, effectively "singing" the failure of the cable. "The pressure makes the fractures dance" became the mantra he screamed while trying to re-seal the main port before the station flooded.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A macro photograph of a glass pane cracking into a thousand fractals, backlit by a dying, deep-sea submarine spotlight, high-contrast, sharp edges, metallic grit.

Track 2: "Where does the pressure end?"
- Story & Context: Mara, the team’s lead diver, sat alone in the airlock after the 400-mile cable snapped, listening to the Prophet-5 hum a low, menacing dissonance that echoed the groaning of the hull. She confessed to her logs that she wasn't repairing the lines anymore, but intentionally stripping the insulation to hear the "static of the abyss" scream through the monitors. "The copper veins are bleeding out my own mistakes" she whispered into the contact mic, her voice clipping into a brutal, digital smear.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A grainy, distorted security camera frame of a woman in a heavy rubber dive suit sitting in a dimly lit, concrete-walled room, staring at a bank of analog dials.

Track 3: The Glazier’s Last Dive
- Story & Context: Legend says the station commander, Elias, tried to fuse the broken data cables with a handmade glass-welding torch, creating a permanent, crystalline scar on the ocean floor. His disappearance remains the primary myth of the scene, with divers claiming that on the anniversary, the cables emit a high-frequency howl that sounds like glass being blown into impossible, jagged shapes. "I poured my lungs into the molten seam" is the final, ghost-tracked vocal hook heard at the end of the song, right before the tape loops into an infinite, grinding feedback.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: An abstract illustration of a human hand holding a glowing, molten glass orb that is rapidly hardening into a sharp, lethal geometric spike, dark ocean tones, embers.

